He does not fall over. CharacterDie in ZzzCharacter.cpp tests the sub-type before it reaches SetAction:

    if (o->SubType >= MODEL_SKELETON1 && o->SubType <= MODEL_SKELETON3)
    {
        o->Live = false;
        CreateEffect(MODEL_BONE1, o->Position, o->Angle, o->Light);
        for (int j = 0; j < 10; j++)
            CreateEffect(MODEL_BONE2, o->Position, o->Angle, o->Light);
        PlayBuffer(SOUND_BONE2, o);
    }
    else
        SetAction(&c->Object, PLAYER_DIE1);

The model is switched off outright and eleven loose bones are thrown where it stood - one large Bone01 and ten small Bone02, out of Data/Skill, with the clatter. He has PLAYER_DIE1 in his rig like every player-rigged thing and never plays it, which is why Crowd hands this figure no die clip at all: a death clip he cannot reach is a clip somebody would one day watch and call wrong. See assets/effects/bones and client/core/Bones.cs for the burst.
